{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790098414,"nonce":"ZfiLwnt4MbQ1p9fOYV5egeZPf60=","message":"Revised 2026-09-22 (f4bac00): the iteration is NOT a separate entity type. It is the owned issue entity (5b09ee1) instantiated in refs/iterations through a second dag.Definition, with its own SubCache. Built-ins there: title, status, archived, and two date fields with roles start and end; capacity is a preset number field with on: iteration, not first class. Create/SetDates/SetCapacity/SetState from aba17f4 are therefore SetField ops on those fields. An issue's membership is a field of kind iteration holding the iteration id. The non-atomic close ordering stands. See configurable-schema.md D5.","files":null}]}